  "body": "The opencode execution lane has never bound a handed-off task through claimant.py: lanes hand off, the claimant fires, and nothing launches. Four defects compounded:\n\n- poll.py json-parsed the repo-queue binary's list output, which is a human table since the #5362 cutover, so every queue read as empty and the gate always exited (#7325, #7375).\n- The checkpoint verb records the yield at progress.last_checkpoint.stage; is_candidate reads progress.stage, so even a working read classified ~0 candidates (#7706).\n- launch_step never read mode — a shadow fire reaching step 4 would have created and bound sessions (#7366) — and it bound sessions without ever sending the execution prompt, manufacturing #4758 zero-message sessions (#7356). Its session calls also carried none of the server's required Basic auth.\n- The broker's rich /list (built for this claimant) did not return the task payload, so launch prompts carried an empty packet.\n\nFixes:\n\n- poll.py reads claimed rows from the broker's /list with rich: true (URL/token resolved exactly as the fleet client resolves them), lifts the yield stage from last_checkpoint, and exposes payload as the candidate packet. Fail-closed semantics unchanged: an unreadable queue contributes no rows.\n- claimant.py supervision reads rows through poll.py; launch_step in shadow mode records the would-launch window as skips and mutates nothing; the live launch creates the session with auth, binds it, then delivers the prompt via POST /api/session/{id}/prompt with message-reconcile before any resend, flagging the launch entry when the prompt cannot be landed. Session responses unwrap the v2 data envelope.\n- fleet-queue: rich /list selects payload on both the Turso and PostgREST paths and parses it as JSON (Turso).\n\nVerification (laptop): python suites 60/60 pass (test_poll + test_claimant, incl. new coverage for the broker read, stage lift, payload packet, shadow no-mutation, prompt-failure flagging and prompt reconcile). Live read-only smoke of the fixed poll.py against the production broker: 22 candidates across the queues (was 0 all day), cap_room 35, no poll warnings.\n\nQueue task 13488 (the claimant-binding fix task; its packet names #1187, the dispatch design this claimant implements).\n\nFixes #7325\nFixes #7375\nFixes #7366\nFixes #7356\nFixes #7706\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796770025&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7834&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7834&signature=6f020e8ec4dd5dbf81fec20e92f498bd8124bc5a823e3374efae29122b8660b2\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7834?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
